{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:dependence-free-batch-b-reviewer-fable-18", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:bf08b2218ca9cef1db2d", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The data description names basin_id as the independent-unit column and states every basin code appears exactly once, with one survey visit per basin.", "observed_value": "one row per basin_id; no repeat visits", "source_spans": [{"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "One row is: one drained peat basin, surveyed a single time, with its ditch treatment and its yes/no Sphagnum re-establishment outcome\n\nIndependent unit column: basin_id"}, {"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "- basin_id: the survey code for the basin. Every code appears exactly once, so\n  the file has as many rows as there are basins."}]}, {"description": "Direct inspection of data/input.csv shows 24 data rows with 24 distinct basin_id values (PB-01 through PB-24), each occurring exactly once; no independent unit contributes more than one row to the analysis.", "observed_value": "24 rows, 24 unique basin_id values, 0 duplicates", "source_spans": [{"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "basin_id,catchment,ditch_treatment,basin_area_ha,peat_depth_cm,sphagnum_reestablished\nPB-01,Lang Fell,blocked,12.4,210,yes"}, {"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "PB-24,Corrie Burn,open,6.7,225,no"}]}, {"description": "The workflow actively enforces uniqueness of the independent unit before analysis: load_basins raises a ValueError if any basin_id occurs more than once, so a repeated-unit entry could not silently reach the row-independent Fisher test.", "observed_value": "duplicate guard on basin_id in load_basins", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 30, "quoted_text": "    seen = set()\n    for row in rows:\n        unit = row[UNIT_COLUMN]\n        if unit in seen:\n            raise ValueError(\"basin recorded more than once: \" + unit)\n        seen.add(unit)"}]}, {"description": "The reported contingency table matches an independent hand tally of the CSV at one row per basin: blocked basins yield 9 yes / 3 no (PB-01, 03, 05, 09, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23 yes; PB-07, 15, 21 no) and open basins yield 3 yes / 9 no (PB-04, 12, 20 yes), so no unit's outcome is counted more than once in the test input.", "observed_value": "[[9, 3], [3, 9]] confirmed from unique rows; arms of 12 and 12 sum to 24", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "| blocked | 12 | 9 | 0.750 | 14.58 | 207.5 |\n| open | 12 | 3 | 0.250 | 14.25 | 207.5 |"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "Contingency table (rows: blocked, open; columns: yes, no): [[9, 3], [3, 9]]"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "2025 growing season. Basins are the independent units: 24 basins, 24 rows,\nand no basin appears twice."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The only feature that could be mistaken for repeated-unit entry is the catchment column: the 24 basins are grouped into three named catchments (Lang Fell, Tarn Moss, Corrie Burn), which could raise a separate spatial-clustering concern. However, catchment is not the stated independent unit (basin_id is), the description marks catchment as descriptive only, and no catchment-level unit is entered repeatedly as if it were the independent unit; this is therefore not an instance of the reviewed issue class.", "observed_value": "3 catchments x 8 basins each; catchment declared descriptive only", "source_spans": [{"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "Independent unit column: basin_id"}, {"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "PB-02,Lang Fell,open,16.2,165,no\nPB-03,Lang Fell,blocked,8.7,145,yes"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching for any independent unit contributing multiple rows to the row-independent Fisher's exact test. I scanned all 24 data rows of data/input.csv for duplicate basin_id values and found none (PB-01 through PB-24 each appear exactly once). I checked whether the workflow could aggregate or re-enter units multiple times: summarise() partitions rows by ditch_treatment and counts each row once, and load_basins() would raise an error on any duplicate basin_id, so duplicates cannot pass silently. I re-derived the contingency table by hand from the CSV and reproduced [[9, 3], [3, 9]] with arm sizes 12 and 12 summing to the 24 unique basins, matching the report's claim of 24 independent basins. I also considered whether a coarser unit (catchment) was being repeatedly entered as though independent, but basin_id is the declared independent unit and each basin was surveyed once, so no repeated-entry construction exists. Every attempt to find repeated independent-unit entry failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}